{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/350574-demonic-faith","id":350574,"title":"Demonic Faith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-26T05:33:57-08:00","id":350574,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Demonic Faith","content":"Ok, I'm still reading DtD, and maybe this question will be answered later in the book... anyway, let me talk about it.<br /> <br /> I've read the Agendas, and though they are broad ways to Descent, it sounds to me that there could be &quot;narrow&quot; tracks inside each one. Like for exemple a group of Demons sharing common insights about how to deCypher their path to Hell. <br /> <br /> I know that Agendas are loosely organizated, but it sounds reasonable that Demons with more similiar visions could congregate among themselves forming &quot;Meta Cults&quot; around those subjects, thus forming more solid groups. That could lead to an interesting and alien concept of &quot;Faith&quot; among Demons.<br /> <br /> Anybody buys it, or paranoia and conspiracy would be sufficient obstacles to hinder such Cults?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","name":"mabafu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T06:32:32-08:00","id":350617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mabafu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/350574-demonic-faith#post350574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody buys it, or paranoia and conspiracy would be sufficient obstacles to hinder such Cults?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't prevent rings and agencies from forming, so there's no reason why they should necessarily prevent this. Rings and Agencies are usually formed around more material interests, rather than beliefs - there's no way for a demon to conclusively demonstrate their sincerity of belief to another - but that also goes for any other declaration of loyalty or interest. So I'd go with yes they can form such cults, though they won't have have quite the same sense of safety and belonging that a human cult might - but they'll have a little, which is still a big comfort to a demon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T07:13:17-08:00","id":350644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/350574-demonic-faith?p=350617#post350617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'd go with yes they can form such cults, though they won't have have quite the same sense of safety and belonging that a human cult might - but they'll have a little, which is still a big comfort to a demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree that a Cult involves things demons lack a lot (i.e. trust, stability, etc.) but when I placed the &quot;Meta&quot; tag on them I meant that faith is something they can grasp only through solving their Cyphers. Something that makes no (or very little) sense at the beggining, but that cames to the &quot;light&quot; as the demons beggins to solve their personal &quot;koans&quot;. Something like Morpheu's faith about Neo being the choosen one at Matrix. It gradually &quot;infects&quot; Neo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />","edited":{"userid":646,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","user":"mabafu","date":". 12-26-2014, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","name":"mabafu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T12:49:05-08:00","id":350857,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that the God-Machine is a scaled element; One ST may want to present it as a straight up deity with some occasional cogs - another may present it as a non-sentient metal system of responses to stimuli. Most will fall somewhere in between.<br /> <br /> If it's the direction you want to go, taking a hard theological interpretation would facilitate this. I mean, you could go so far as to define Faith (in something other than the God-Machine) as the actual mechanic of the fall - when an Angel has a crisis of Faith - or a moment of doubt, it is forever cast out. As their faith grows, it renders them epiphanies called interlocks and reveals their own path of faith - their cypher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4576-darthdoctor","name":"DarthDoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T13:02:56-08:00","id":353018,"title":"","content":"Well.. the <b>techgnosticism </b>is always and very present in the book (and I didn't ever finished it yet), but it seems to me that in the core the apeal is more stylistic (<b>tech</b>). The designers had gave us a lot of hints about their visions about GM's &quot;cogs&quot;, &quot;machinery&quot;, and somekind of a neo-cyber-steam-punk stylish outlook of the setting. Agendas, as I see it, came to deal with the conceptual aspect of the game (<b>gnosticism</b>). But there a lot of &quot;gaps&quot; between each term, that, I believe, were left to us to weave together (or, at least until Agenda Manuals begin to be realeased).<br /> <br /> Well, after all, the book gave us a lot of freedom about dealing with Demons, and their innate ability to &quot;deviate&quot; from the &quot;cannon&quot; (I remember reading it scattered in some paragraphs of the book). To specialize Agendas, or to give them layers of &quot;loyalty&quot; based uppon &quot;Faith&quot; would be an easy take of mine about the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","name":"mabafu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}